e two of them end up in the  stables the plan here is that hitch  would quietly take the female titan  outside of the district and during this  conversation we got an insight into what  it's like to live inside a crystal  the way annie describes it it's like her  state of partial consciousness where she  could hear what's happening around her  but other than that it was basically  like a dark dream all that time the only  company she had was amis news updates  and hitch ranting about men so it is a  miracle that annie hasn't turned out any  crazier than she used to be  as they leave town we see more of the  carnage as people mourn their dead  relatives and hitch makes an interesting  observation that her only meaningful  work has been cleaning up after the  destruction generally speaking that  statement is probably true for most mps  since their jobs usually don't involve  improving humanity in fact for most of  their existence they were used by the  king to prevent humanity from  progressing for that reason you can see  why hitch would find some meaning in  helping people to rebuild after these  disasters and the first time she had to  do it was after aaron and annie tore up  stoics  moving on they then have an honest  discussion about annie's motivations and  this added a ton of context to our  actions in the first season to start  things off we find out that annie was  abandoned as a baby by her real parents  since just like reina she was the result  of an affair between an aldian and a  regular human because of that she was  adopted by mr leinhardt who himself was  an alien from a foreign country he knew  that by raising annie to become a  warrior it would give him the title of  honorary marlian and all the benefits  that come with that and so during her  childhood he aggressively trained her in  the martial arts from his homeland  the endless practicing and physical  abuse made it so that she eventually saw  no value in any life whether it was her  own life the lives of animals or the  lives of the soldiers she had to kill  from her perspective none of it had any  meaning and as a consequence she also  didn't care about saving the world like  the other warrior candidates did  anyway once she grew up strong enough  she beat up mr leinhardt to repay him  for all the suffering he put her through  and this beat down was so bad that he  received permanent damage to his knee  explaining why he's usually seen with a  walking stick  after then graduating to become a fully  fledged warrior she was then chosen for  the invasion of paradise and the morning  of her deployment is when mr leinhardt  dropped to his knees and apologized for  everything he'd done this moment here is  a more detailed version of this  flashback from the first season as it  does a better job of conveying just how  devastated he was although he'd never  shown his true feelings until this  moment he did in fact view annie as his  real daughter and to him the title of  honorary malian didn't mean anything if  she never returned from the island it  was only once she heard this speech and  looked into his eyes that she realized  how much he cared and from that point  onwards it became her singular  motivation to make it back home alive  this motivation has been demonstrated  many times for example when marcel was  eating it was annie who suggested they  should go back home and while stomping  out rainer she made it clear how  desperate she was to return to mali  alive  then a few years later when they were  inside the walls it was annie again who  suggested they should go back without  completing their mission  she's also the warrior who arguably put  in the most work into locating the  founder so they could go home and those  tears when she was captured was because  she wasn't able to fulfill her promise  now in the present day annie accepts  that her previous view on life having no  value was wrong and that all the deaths  she caused wasn't really justified  ho