e in this new world the aegis are  creating which is the reason why he let  them beat him up charlize knew that  someone like him was never going to make  it regardless of what happened but if  his cadets joined the yagaris then  they'll survive until one day they can  start a revolution  this ties into what hanus was saying  last season in that when one group takes  over from another it's only a matter of  time until the cycle of revolution  eventually repeats again  now in the changing room armin is  getting ready for a trip to ragako  village as he's determined to try and  stop connie from feeding falco to his  mother his aim in doing this isn't  simply to save falco as i'm pretty sure  those two have never had a conversation  but rather he's doing this to earn  gabby's trust if gabi trusts armin then  it might be possible for the scouts to  use that trust to ease their conflict  with reiner and peak who are both still  somewhere on the island as he goes to  leave mikasa asks him what they should  do about eren and this is when armin  loses it at her possibly for the first  time ever the reason he snaps is because  of all the things going on right now  aaron is dead last when it comes to what  they should be dealing with for example  nobody knows where levi and hanji are  annie is back the volunteers that have  helped them for years are now in trouble  and there's an unknown number of  casualties on the island on top of that  the queen is possibly in danger as right  now they have no idea what the aegir is  planned to do with her  with all that going on no one is in any  position to be thinking about aaron  hence why armin lost his composure at  the question he then goes on to riley  point out that commander aaron wouldn't  have reacted in the same way and follows  this by admitting that he wasn't the one  who levi should have saved  if we flash back to 4 years ago no one  was realistically expecting the  commander to be replaced but one thing  levi asked of armin was that he didn't  make himself or anyone else regret the  choice that was meant to be his  responsibility going forward but now we  can say that it's a responsibility that  he's definitely failed in crisis  situations like this evan always remain  level-headed even when other people were  losing it and this distinction between  the two is why armin feels the way he  does  anyhow as armin lee's mikasa notices her  scarf is missing and the last time we  saw it she left it alone in this room  with her number one stalker  things then briefly switched to outside  where nicolo and the brass family say  their last goodbyes to gabby since it's  unclear if they'll ever see the warrior  candidate again as we know gabby and  armin's current mission is to make it to  ragako village before falco gets eaten  but beyond that we know her motivation  is to stop aaron from rumbling the world  therefore there's a decent chance that  her time on parodies might be coming to  an end very soon which is why this whole  interaction felt very final  back inside the four we see the  volunteers have been rounded up just  like flock wanted in the last episode  and this moment helps to explain why  aaron left him in charge of the yagaris  ten months ago we already knew that  aaron and elena had a secret meeting  where she told him about the  euthanization plan and flock is the one  who enabled that meeting to happen  soon after this aaron revealed to flock  that he planned to betray zeke and ever  since then flock has been gathering  allies which is why the aegis was so  strong in numbers and well organized as  soon as the revolution began  with the rumbling now underway pretty  much everything has gone the way they  intended but being the psycho that he is  flock mocks the volunteers for their  homelands being destroyed a lot of these  volunteers are from countries that were  invaded by mali and they helped paradise  because they thought it would weaken the  malians and therefore benefit th