falca  were heading towards ragako on horseback  and the two main things we need to  understand from this interaction is that  number one falco has no idea he's  inherited the draw titan in the past  we've seen that new time shifters  usually forget the events surrounding  how they got their power and in falco's  case the last thing he remembers is  being with colton gabby this means that  he doesn't know his brother is dead he  doesn't know galliard is dead and he  also doesn't seem to be aware of the  rumbling  point number two is that connie took  advantage of this memory loss by making  up a fake story and now the young  warrior believes that he's being taken  to a hospital the credits then finished  with falco feeling like he's seen connie  somewhere before and this is referring  to the airship where the warrior  candidates definitely would have seen  him in particular there was one moment  where he dramatically opened the door to  announce sasha's death and gabby and  falca were both in the room at that time  things then move over to general mcgath  and the cart titan who watch on as the  remaining malian airships leave them  behind with the rumbling marching  towards the continent these ships are  going to warn everyone about what's  happening but mcgath acknowledges  there's nothing anyone can actually do  to stop the destruction the car titan  then reacts as hanji approaches them  from behind and this is the first time  we've seen the commander since the first  episode of part two in that time she's  managed to steal a horse and fix up  captain levi who is very much alive  despite not being in the best shape  now you might be wondering what hanji  would gain from approaching pekin mcgath  in this way and the answer is that at  this moment both sides sort of want to  achieve the same thing  to be more specific levi wants to kill  zeke which is something the general has  tried to do several times and hanji  doesn't agree with aaron destroying all  life on the planet which is something  that no malian wants to happen by  combining their forces it would make  achieving those goals at least a bit  more plausible and this potential  alliance should be explored in more  detail next week  anyway people that was my breakdown for  episode 23 of attack on titan season 4  and if it helped you to understand the  episode in any way then i'd appreciate  if you dropped a like and let me know  your thoughts in the comments down below  also don't forget to check out this  special link in the description to  download dragon city and get your free  rewards  thanks for watching the video as always  and until the next one peace out
 

